{"id":"5d8152f660ee553b89b2cb77","source":"oryx-web","source_name":"Oryx","platform":"web","url":"https://www.oryxspioenkop.com/2014/02/","published_at":null,"collected_at":"2026-10-23T00:13:58.832196Z","title":"February 2014 - Oryx","text":", North Korean Helical AK Magazines Anonymous DPRK , Helical magazine 0 Comments By Joost Oliemans and Stijn Mitzer Several new developments in North Korean armaments can be witnessed amongst the recent flow of propaganda released by Pyongyang after Kim Jong Un's ascension to power. One such development is what appears to be a new magazine model for the North Korean copy of the AK-74, the Type 88. This new magazine uses a staggered helix design, which allows for a high number of 5.45 x 39 mm cartridges to be carried without the notable increases in size and unwieldiness that characterise many other high capacity magazines. Share Twitter Facebook Read More","html":"","media":["https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjx6w9uLeezke541U011kxfsa6KQwSpCKcu8vXPx6C11V0p3z1tQ_yAa9JEWZH4hhm8XQnsz6QJMK47RGweGbrHrAPazzUftwFgjIcqieUT9H43JZrCl4jsU81ZacHDYavxXXy1v3bnNZOs/s16000/Helical.jpg"],"author":"Oryx","language":"und","group":"osint","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"662a45a427655f01246af467b11d4c6acf74affd0088550fadb35546e400421f","original_text_chars":663,"original_html_chars":3721,"text_truncated":false,"media_count":1,"platform":{"content_type":"web_article"}}}
